{"name":"prip","description":"Runcitruncated 5-cell (prismatorhombated pentachoron)","source":"topology_output/prip.json","format":"polychoron-modal/1","model":{"body":"thin-walled hollow 4D body: the cells are welded 3D plates of thickness h","equations":"Kirchhoff bending of each cell along its 4D normal, (h^3/12)[lam* (Lap w)^2 + 2 mu |grad grad w|^2], lam* = 2 lam mu/(lam+2mu); ridges fixed (thin-wall limit), hinge rotation continuous across ridges (welded)","method":"Ritz per cell with two bubbles: phi = (sum_f d_f^-2)^(-1/2), a smooth distance to the face planes, and b = prod_f tanh(d_f/delta); phi^2 x poly (zero slope at the faces: the interior) plus phi x poly and b x poly for the hinge rotations (near an edge they behave like r and r^2, the exact solution like r^(pi/alpha) in between). Soft walls: slopes p - 2, interior p; stiff walls resonating in the range: slopes 6, interior 4; the others: phi x poly slopes 6, interior 2 (see basis; polynomial_degree lists p for soft walls, the slope degree for stiff ones). Legendre-product polynomials, orthonormalised by QR; cell matrices per shape mapped by congruence; problem block-diagonalised by (Z2)^2 mirror symmetries (one block per character, assembled from one representative cell per orbit); hinge penalty beta = 1000 mu h^3 / l","polynomial_degree":{"cuboctahedron":8,"hexagonal prism":8,"triangular prism":6,"truncated tetrahedron":8},"basis":{"cuboctahedron":"both: slopes 6, interior 8","hexagonal prism":"both: slopes 6, interior 8","triangular prism":"both: slopes 6, interior 4","truncated tetrahedron":"both: slopes 6, interior 8"},"computed_up_to":"5 x f1 (plus the band reaching over it)","lambda_over_mu":1.0,"units":"circumradius R = 1, density rho = 1, shear modulus mu = 1 (shear wave speed c_s = 1); wall thickness h_ref = 0.06 R","frequency":"f_Hz = frequency * (h / h_ref) * c_s[m/s] / R[m]  (bending: f ~ h)","gains":"as in modal_output (mass-relative, per multiplet sum); mean = multiplicity (every mode bends all its mass); tangential = 0 and no vertex gains (membrane motion is not modelled, ridges and vertices are fixed)","rel_error":"indicator: change of the modes of two symmetry blocks when every degree is lowered by 2 (per multiplet the largest change of its members, else of the nearest mode); pessimistic: the step from these degrees to 2 higher is several times smaller. Ritz values are upper bounds","multiplet_merge_tol":1e-05},"geometry":{"boundary_volume":13.2738352,"edge_length":0.6201736723,"counts":[60,150,120,30]},"modes":{"frequency":[0.20885027,0.23096303,0.24816852,0.25092843,0.26973629,0.30275604,0.33311845,0.38724904,0.38877513,0.393806,0.41174548,0.44958437,0.45200357,0.45427054,0.47052115,0.47068182,0.48517288,0.56967814,0.57668384,0.58584867,0.58817875,0.61593308,0.61822811,0.63539334,0.63793605,0.65145757,0.66947616,0.68086481,0.68239931,0.68648595,0.69904455,0.70221365,0.70575233,0.7094332,0.74393925,0.74874709,0.75437388,0.75462517,0.75956347,0.78395486,0.78888836,0.79529419,0.80216324,0.80268885,0.82000746,0.82123054,0.85066063,0.85074598,0.85163216,0.88023042,0.90364176,0.92065372,0.93365972,0.94467906,0.95357702,0.95848479,0.96104473,0.96491001,0.9695385,0.9766293,0.98357351,0.98827631,0.99576061,0.99624382,0.99826612,1.0094891,1.0110749,1.0185343,1.0225972,1.0302814,1.0359311,1.0407041,1.0438253,1.0513057,1.0522589,1.0549989,1.0657337,1.0674165,1.0808734,1.0818646,1.0856436,1.090935,1.0964646,1.1022395,1.1181168],"multiplicity":[1,4,4,1,5,4,1,4,5,6,5,6,4,5,5,6,4,4,5,5,6,1,4,5,6,4,5,4,5,6,5,1,4,5,5,6,5,4,1,6,4,4,4,6,4,5,1,5,5,5,4,6,6,5,4,5,1,4,5,4,6,5,1,4,5,6,4,5,4,5,6,6,4,5,1,4,4,6,5,4,4,6,5,5,6],"rel_error":[0.0022,0.014,0.047,0.036,0.026,0.0082,0.0011,0.011,0.055,0.05,0.053,0.04,0.048,0.049,0.053,0.059,0.027,0.042,0.065,0.099,0.094,0.037,0.041,0.06,0.075,0.053,0.072,0.054,0.064,0.08,0.063,0.056,0.053,0.084,0.08,0.089,0.082,0.08,0.075,0.074,0.084,0.06,0.11,0.11,0.075,0.1,0.051,0.076,0.14,0.14,0.11,0.15,0.17,0.17,0.14,0.16,0.15,0.15,0.15,0.14